Fluxyr Agent includes code extracted and adapted from Fluxyr (fluxyr-work2),
commit 019eceb0b82ccc955280671a6813ba602cc70c0a, at the owner's request.
Preserved modules include SyntheticBrain, model adapters, tool batch policies,
human decision gate, web content extraction, TechDoc and vault encryption.

The frontend incorporates and adapts Scificn UI components published for
copy-paste integration at https://www.scificn.dev/ by baxy5:
Button, Badge, Panel, Card, Input, Textarea, Label, Select, Checkbox, Switch,
Separator, StatusGrid, Typography, Breadcrumb, Dialog and Spinner.
Retrieved 2026-10-07.
Theme source revision: 8b06737dcfbf38c55236b7a6b77f15070c5bb3fd.
Registry file digests are recorded in frontend/src/ui/scificn-source.json.
Local adaptations include Fluxyr design tokens, locally hosted fonts,
accessible dialog close labeling, unique form-control IDs, Scificn Label usage,
bounded dropdown height, corrected Switch state-label selectors and the branded
rounded symbol. Application adapters preserve empty/numeric select values and
share execution status labels without changing backend states.

Bundled IBM Plex Mono and Inter fonts are distributed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. Their copyright and license texts are in frontend/public/licenses
and included in the packaged UI.

PDF previews use Mozilla PDF.js (pdfjs-dist), distributed under the Apache
License 2.0. Its license is included in frontend/public/licenses/PDFjs-LICENSE
and in the packaged UI. The viewer and worker are served locally.

The optional browser controller integrates public-browser 3.0.0 by Silbercue.
Its tool-schemas.json is generated from the public-browser tool catalogue.
The MIT license is included at fluxyr/browser_runtime/PUBLIC_BROWSER_LICENSE.txt.
